I agree.

267
00:17:18,119 --> 00:17:19,119
Okay.

268
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:21,359
- Tungtae!
- Tae!

269
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:23,000
- Go ahead, little Bro.
- Tungtae!

270
00:17:23,079 --> 00:17:25,599
Come on, tell your boss the good news.

271
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:26,720
What queue number did you get?

272
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:27,960
Number one, Bro.

273
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:32,360
- You're amazing.
- Number one hundred, Bro.

274
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:35,320
- You little punk.
- Want to fight me?

275
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:37,440
One hundred?

276
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:40,320
I sent you so early,
and you still got number 100?

277
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,800
There were too many people. I did my best.

278
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:45,160
Let's grab something to eat.

279
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:47,280
- This line is insanely long.
- Yeah.

280
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:48,640
Seriously, I'm getting hungry.

281
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:49,760
Come on.

282
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:52,400
- Don't blame the kid.
- I rushed here first thing.

283
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:56,040
- Number 25.
- What?

284
00:17:56,120 --> 00:17:57,120
- Number 25.
- Only 25 so far?

285
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,520
Only number 25?

286
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:14,080
Who's that?

287
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:20,160
Hey, that's Newyear.

288
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,200
Newyear?

289
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:23,320
- Newyear!
- Hey, Newyear!

290
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:26,040
- Newyear!
- Newyear!

291
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:28,800
Even Newyear came to Jia for a reading.

292
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,480
- Newyear.
- Let's go.

293
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:33,960
Number 100.

294
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:36,840
This has to be the place.

295
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:37,960
Go on, have a seat.

296
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:40,120
- You're the one getting the reading.
- Sit down.

297
00:18:42,800 --> 00:18:43,960
Hang in there.

298
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:45,640
Once you see the fortune teller,

299
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:46,880
you'll feel better.

300
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:49,040
- You'll be fine. Trust me.
- Yeah, trust him.

301
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:50,400
But I don't know.

302
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:53,560
The only one I want is Faye,
not a fortune teller.

303
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:58,400
- Hey, wait.
- Hold on.

304
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:00,480
- You haven't had your fortune read yet.
- Jia's here.

305
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:15,040
Damn, he's a real fashion icon.

306
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:16,320
Sit down.

307
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:17,600
Why are you all standing over me?

308
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:20,960
- You.
- Go on.

309
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:22,120
You're getting your fortune read.

310
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,600
Date of birth?

311
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:31,840
Tell him.

312
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:32,880
Why are you looking at me?

313
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:35,960
March 7th, 2009.

314
00:19:50,040 --> 00:19:51,560
You were just in an accident, weren't you?

315
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:55,000
What?

316
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:58,160
A love accident?

317
00:19:58,240 --> 00:20:00,000
Something you never saw coming.

318
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:04,320
You got hurt in the head and it cracked.

319
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:06,800
Your "heart."

320
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:08,120
That's what he meant.

321
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:10,800
Is he really that accurate?

322
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,040
He is.

323
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:13,640
Exactly.

324
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:14,720
Or maybe because his eyes are closed,

325
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:16,440
he can't see our reactions

326
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:17,920
to know he got everything wrong.

327
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:21,280
Dream.

328
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:25,240
You dream of becoming a pilot.

329
00:20:25,320 --> 00:20:26,280
That'll be difficult.

330
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:31,720
- I…
- Hey.

331
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:34,040
I've never wanted to be a pilot.

332
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:37,240
I think he's just making things up.

333
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:38,840
Indy's terrified of flying.

334
00:20:40,440 --> 00:20:42,480
I don't think fortune-telling is for me.

335
00:20:42,560 --> 00:20:44,440
- I'm leaving.
- Let's go.

336
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:46,160
- He's totally making it up.
- Hey.

337
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:48,240
Wait, wait.

338
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:49,360
At least give him a chance.

339
00:20:50,440 --> 00:20:51,840
He might miss with cold readings,

340
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:53,800
but tarot is his signature.

341
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:55,680
Give him a chance.

342
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:57,880
- What's with you?
- Let him draw the cards first.

343
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:59,520
- Trust me.
- Fine, just this once.

344
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:00,560
Trust me.

345
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:02,800
You just got your heart broken
by someone older, didn't you?

346
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:07,240
Shit.

347
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:08,880
- Told you.
- Spot on.

348
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:10,560
- Sit down.
- You.

349
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:11,600
Yes.

350
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:19,840
You were really hurt.

351
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:21,800
The cards also say

352
00:21:21,880 --> 00:21:23,080
that person has a high profile,

353
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:26,000
like an emperor. The best of the best.

354
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:29,880
Spot on.

355
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:33,120
See? I told you.

356
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:38,320
Shuffle the cards
if you want to know more.

357
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:55,560
Come on.

358
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:58,000
Give one to him.

359
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:09,320
The love you hoped for won't come true.

360
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,560
But the love you're
not looking for is close by.

361
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:13,480
Simply put,

362
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:15,440
it's someone in your class.

363
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:18,600
Who is it?

364
00:22:24,240 --> 00:22:25,480
Excuse me, fortune teller.

365
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,200
What's he doing?

366
00:22:31,800 --> 00:22:32,800
No idea.

367
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:39,800
I want to ask about my studies.

368
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:42,080
Will I get into architecture school?

369
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:44,120
These cards aren't about your studies.

370
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:45,680
They're about love.

371
00:22:47,960 --> 00:22:50,040
Someone's about to confess to you.

372
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:54,160
And if you date,

373
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:56,960
it's going to be amazing.

374
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:58,080
A total hit.

375
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:02,800
Is it the one you have a crush on?

376
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:05,120
Who is it, fortune teller?

377
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:07,560
I can't tell you.

378
00:23:08,080 --> 00:23:09,240
That's all the cards reveal.

379
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:10,720
When the time comes,

380
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:11,840
the truth will reveal itself.

381
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:15,000
<i>Why am I even getting worked up?</i>

382
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:21,440
Actually, you can get another reading.

383
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:23,840
One reading per person.

384
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:25,000
JIA'S SHRINE

385
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:27,040
Damn it, you're missing the point.

386
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:28,440
We're here for Indy's reading.

387
00:23:29,120 --> 00:23:30,280
Come on, let's step outside.

388
00:23:30,360 --> 00:23:31,840
Give them some privacy.

389
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:34,400
So they can talk in peace.

390
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:36,280
Come on, you've got this.

391
00:23:36,360 --> 00:23:37,600
Don't overthink it.

392
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:39,840
Ask him whatever you want.

393
00:23:39,920 --> 00:23:40,880
Go, go, go.

394
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:42,120
You too.

395
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:43,320
Take your bag.

396
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:50,080
Now it's your turn.

397
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:54,440
I…

398
00:23:54,520 --> 00:23:56,080
want to move on.

399
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:57,280
How do I do that?

400
00:24:13,840 --> 00:24:16,280
The cards say
you need to try something new.

401
00:24:16,360 --> 00:24:17,640
That's hard.

402
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:20,840
Everything I do reminds me of her.

403
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:28,160
Actually, joining the initiation ritual
will definitely help.

404
00:24:30,400 --> 00:24:31,920
If you're interested, message me.

405
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:35,560
JIRAKORN RERKSAKONRAT

406
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:38,600
I am. I'm interested.

407
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:41,720
Then the first Saturday after finals.

408
00:24:42,400 --> 00:24:45,880
- Okay.
- At exactly 12:25 p.m.

409
00:24:45,960 --> 00:24:46,920
I'll send you the location.

410
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:51,320
For the remaining 30 minutes,
ask me anything.

411
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:03,680
You're very hardworking.

412
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:05,640
You don't need the cards. You'll get in.

413
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:09,520
You never know.

414
00:25:09,600 --> 00:25:11,040
There could be lots of people
who work harder than me.

415
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:16,000
Oh, right.

416
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:17,720
About what the fortune teller said…

417
00:25:18,320 --> 00:25:20,600
That someone would confess to you.

418
00:25:20,680 --> 00:25:21,840
Anyone come to mind?

419
00:25:23,320 --> 00:25:24,920
You seem more curious than I am.

420
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:28,960
Maybe I'm just being nosy.

421
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:41,560
Damn, that's awesome.

422
00:25:41,640 --> 00:25:42,600
What's this called again?

423
00:25:42,680 --> 00:25:44,160
This one?

424
00:25:44,240 --> 00:25:46,040
It's called line practice.

425
00:25:47,040 --> 00:25:48,480
It's for controlling pressure.

426
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:50,320
And training hand-eye coordination.

427
00:25:53,840 --> 00:25:55,000
How long have you been practicing?

428
00:25:57,280 --> 00:25:59,360
- About three years, I guess.
- Damn.

429
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:01,320
That's as long as
I've been playing guitar.

430
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:02,680
But damn,

431
00:26:02,760 --> 00:26:04,280
I still can't hit the right chords.

432
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:07,440
I've thrown away plenty of sketches too.

433
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:11,120
Can I see?

434
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:17,720
No.

435
00:26:24,280 --> 00:26:25,120
It's beautiful.

436
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:30,880
Wait.

437
00:26:31,480 --> 00:26:32,760
Can you draw me?

438
00:26:32,840 --> 00:26:35,040
No. Drawing people is hard.

439
00:26:35,120 --> 00:26:36,480
There are too many details.

440
00:26:38,240 --> 00:26:40,240
It can't be harder
than the buildings you draw.

441
00:26:40,320 --> 00:26:42,040
Whatever these are.
What's with all these pillars?

442
00:26:44,200 --> 00:26:45,520
Please.

443
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:47,320
You won't know until you try. Please.

444
00:26:47,400 --> 00:26:49,000
People show their emotions.

445
00:26:50,160 --> 00:26:51,320
I'm still a beginner.

446
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:52,680
Please.

447
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:54,520
Will you draw me?

448
00:26:56,880 --> 00:26:57,840
So you will?

449
00:26:57,920 --> 00:26:59,600
Yeah, I'll draw you.

450
00:27:02,120 --> 00:27:04,640
So, how still do I have to sit?

451
00:27:06,480 --> 00:27:08,640
As still as you can.

452
00:27:09,640 --> 00:27:10,640
And,

453
00:27:11,560 --> 00:27:12,520
where should I look?

454
00:27:12,600 --> 00:27:13,720
Over there?

455
00:27:14,640 --> 00:27:15,480
You can look at me.

456
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:20,600
Stay still.

457
00:27:35,080 --> 00:27:37,240
<i>Then date me.</i>

458
00:27:37,320 --> 00:27:38,480
<i>Shit.</i>

459
00:27:38,560 --> 00:27:39,680
<i>That voice is back.</i>

460
00:27:40,280 --> 00:27:41,480
Hey.

461
00:27:41,560 --> 00:27:43,280
You're fidgeting too much.

462
00:27:43,360 --> 00:27:44,520
Sit a little more still.

463
00:27:45,120 --> 00:27:46,400
Okay, okay.

464
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:49,840
<i>Don't let that voice win.</i>

465
00:27:49,920 --> 00:27:51,520
<i>You made that rule yourself.</i>

466
00:27:51,600 --> 00:27:53,320
<i>And he already likes someone.</i>

467
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:54,720
<i>Besides,</i>

468
00:27:54,800 --> 00:27:56,680
<i>it's someone really close to him.</i>

469
00:28:33,280 --> 00:28:34,360
Done.

470
00:28:39,520 --> 00:28:41,080
Whoa, that was fast.

471
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:42,440
You're Picasso.

472
00:28:43,360 --> 00:28:45,200
See? I told you.

473
00:28:47,680 --> 00:28:48,800
Wait, wait.

474
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:50,680
- Can I…
- What?

475
00:28:50,760 --> 00:28:51,960
Can I have the drawing?

476
00:28:52,040 --> 00:28:54,120
Please. I want it.

477
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:56,120
Keep it and it'll give you nightmares.

478
00:28:57,600 --> 00:28:58,800
Probably.

479
00:29:00,680 --> 00:29:02,320
You could at least encourage me.

480
00:29:03,400 --> 00:29:04,480
Come on.

481
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:07,680
Here, once you've done more drawings,

482
00:29:07,760 --> 00:29:10,160
I'm sure you'll get much better.

483
00:29:11,160 --> 00:29:12,000
Just keep drawing me.

484
00:29:12,080 --> 00:29:14,120
Draw my face over and over.

485
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:16,680
When you make a better version,

486
00:29:16,760 --> 00:29:18,240
you can trade it for this one.

487
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:21,840
Mm.

488
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:27,080
Wait.

489
00:29:27,600 --> 00:29:28,720
Sign this for me.

490
00:29:29,360 --> 00:29:30,520
Right here.

491
00:29:32,240 --> 00:29:33,720
Why do I have to sign?

492
00:29:35,960 --> 00:29:37,080
Here.

493
00:29:37,160 --> 00:29:38,440
Why do I have to sign?

494
00:29:38,520 --> 00:29:40,560
The blood pact is sealed now.

495
00:29:41,320 --> 00:29:42,720
I'll wait until you're famous.

496
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:44,120
Puttcasso.

497
00:29:45,800 --> 00:29:47,000
You're so lame.

498
00:29:53,680 --> 00:29:59,840
SEMESTER BREAK

499
00:30:11,600 --> 00:30:13,400
How am I supposed to know?

500
00:30:33,360 --> 00:30:35,200
How am I supposed to know?

501
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:44,360
- Hello.
- Turn left.

502
00:30:49,080 --> 00:30:51,360
There's no way I'd miss you.

503
00:30:51,440 --> 00:30:53,160
You're basically a landmark.

504
00:31:00,280 --> 00:31:01,320
The timing is perfect.

505
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:03,080
Where's the ritual, fortune teller?

506
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:04,400
Right here.

507
00:31:05,480 --> 00:31:06,680
Ready?

508
00:31:07,200 --> 00:31:09,080
Ready to make a wish?

509
00:31:09,160 --> 00:31:11,440
May only good things come your way.

510
00:31:13,960 --> 00:31:14,960
Let's go.

511
00:31:16,280 --> 00:31:18,040
The first ritual starts here.

512
00:31:19,240 --> 00:31:21,120
In a barbershop, fortune teller?

513
00:31:22,000 --> 00:31:23,320
Just call me Jia.

514
00:31:23,400 --> 00:31:24,880
I meant to tell you that day.

515
00:31:24,960 --> 00:31:26,600
Call me whatever but that.

516
00:31:27,760 --> 00:31:29,080
Alright then.

517
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:32,040
Hurry up. I booked your slot.

518
00:31:32,120 --> 00:31:33,720
If we're late, we'll lose it.

519
00:31:34,560 --> 00:31:35,880
The 12:25 slot.

520
00:31:35,960 --> 00:31:37,600
This is a haircut appointment?

521
00:31:38,160 --> 00:31:39,560
Don't question the fortune teller,

522
00:31:39,640 --> 00:31:41,120
or you'll jinx me.

523
00:31:49,720 --> 00:31:50,720
How is it?

524
00:31:51,800 --> 00:31:53,320
I feel like a new person.

525
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:56,880
We're not done yet.

526
00:31:56,960 --> 00:31:59,280
- Really? What's next?
- Come on. Let's go.

527
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:03,920
Damn, this feels so weird.

528
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:13,480
You need something new.

529
00:32:14,480 --> 00:32:15,560
When you find something new,

530
00:32:15,640 --> 00:32:17,400
it's easier to let go of the past.

531
00:32:18,200 --> 00:32:19,400
Really, fortune teller?

532
00:32:22,120 --> 00:32:23,600
You can burn this outfit tomorrow.

533
00:32:24,360 --> 00:32:25,400
But for today,

534
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:29,000
wear it, and pretend

535
00:32:31,360 --> 00:32:32,800
you're someone else.

536
00:32:42,800 --> 00:32:44,280
Something like that.

537
00:32:46,280 --> 00:32:47,560
Let's go.

538
00:32:47,640 --> 00:32:49,200
Go where?

539
00:32:49,280 --> 00:32:50,400
There's more?

540
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:52,400
Get ready to sweat.

541
00:32:52,480 --> 00:32:53,800
You've cried enough already. Let's go.

542
00:33:45,360 --> 00:33:46,280
There you go.

543
00:33:50,560 --> 00:33:51,440
How do you feel?

544
00:33:55,760 --> 00:33:57,080
I feel great.

545
00:33:58,320 --> 00:34:01,000
You've released all that old energy.

546
00:34:02,760 --> 00:34:03,600
Next,

547
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:06,320
delete every contact named Faye.

548
00:34:09,159 --> 00:34:10,639
Do I really have to go that far?

549
00:34:12,280 --> 00:34:13,280
According to the belief,

550
00:34:13,360 --> 00:34:16,040
change starts by letting go of the old.

551
00:34:16,120 --> 00:34:18,120
So there's room for something new.

552
00:34:18,199 --> 00:34:19,600
This is the final step.

553
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:22,840
Your phone, please.

554
00:34:31,199 --> 00:34:32,639
It's like cleaning your house.

555
00:34:32,719 --> 00:34:34,159
If you don't throw old things away,

556
00:34:34,239 --> 00:34:36,159
there won't be room for anything new.

557
00:34:39,719 --> 00:34:44,280
FAYE.NAREEYA - FOLLOWING

558
00:34:47,280 --> 00:34:48,239
Fine.

559
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:49,320
Let's do it.

560
00:34:50,560 --> 00:34:51,400
UNFOLLOW

561
00:34:51,480 --> 00:34:53,440
FOLLOW

562
00:34:55,159 --> 00:34:56,600
It will feel empty at first.

563
00:34:58,720 --> 00:34:59,640
Damn.

564
00:34:59,720 --> 00:35:01,080
It really does.

565
00:35:01,160 --> 00:35:02,440
Now I'm sad again.

566
00:35:04,680 --> 00:35:06,200
Then don't fight it.

567
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:08,560
If you're sad,
be as sad as you need to be.

568
00:36:16,280 --> 00:36:17,520
That's enough.

569
00:36:18,200 --> 00:36:19,640
My hair's a bird's nest now.

570
00:36:20,680 --> 00:36:22,040
A bird's nest?

571
00:36:22,120 --> 00:36:24,080
Come here. I'll fix it.

572
00:36:30,200 --> 00:36:32,320
So, do you feel better?

573
00:36:34,160 --> 00:36:35,560
Yeah, I do.

574
00:36:35,640 --> 00:36:37,200
It feels strangely good.

575
00:36:37,920 --> 00:36:39,600
Mostly strange.

576
00:36:39,680 --> 00:36:41,720
Told you it would work.

577
00:36:42,840 --> 00:36:45,000
Yeah. It really did.

578
00:36:46,880 --> 00:36:47,880
So,

579
00:36:48,760 --> 00:36:50,520
are you going anywhere now?

580
00:36:52,440 --> 00:36:53,400
I'm free.

581
00:36:53,480 --> 00:36:55,080
My client just canceled.

582
00:36:56,600 --> 00:36:57,600
Really?

583
00:36:59,960 --> 00:37:01,000
Then come with me.

584
00:37:01,080 --> 00:37:03,240
Want to see my friends play?

585
00:37:03,840 --> 00:37:04,840
Sure.

586
00:37:12,600 --> 00:37:15,160
Didn't Indy and Tungtae come with you?

587
00:37:15,240 --> 00:37:16,240
Oh,

588
00:37:17,240 --> 00:37:19,080
Tae's doing something with his mom.

589
00:37:19,160 --> 00:37:21,800
As for Indy, he's busy trying to move on.

590
00:37:21,880 --> 00:37:23,120
Move on?

591
00:37:23,800 --> 00:37:24,960
Ask him yourself.

592
00:37:25,040 --> 00:37:26,600
Though I don't know if they'll show up.

593
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:32,040
Hey, Proud's about to go on.

594
00:37:32,120 --> 00:37:33,600
Ready to cheer?

595
00:37:33,680 --> 00:37:34,760
Are you ready?

596
00:37:34,840 --> 00:37:37,720
No. Putter dragged me here.

597
00:37:37,800 --> 00:37:39,440
I'm actually here to cheer
for someone else.

598
00:37:40,040 --> 00:37:41,680
You two need to make up already.

599
00:37:41,760 --> 00:37:43,800
How long are you going to keep this up?

600
00:37:43,880 --> 00:37:45,360
- Are they fake fighting?
- I don't even know her.

601
00:37:45,440 --> 00:37:46,600
That's what I thought.

602
00:37:47,520 --> 00:37:50,200
When will Lazy Meow Meow
get to perform like everyone else?

603
00:37:51,640 --> 00:37:54,320
When people stop saying I play like crap.

604
00:37:55,200 --> 00:37:57,360
Hey, you're really good,

605
00:37:57,440 --> 00:37:58,400
I'm serious.

606
00:37:58,480 --> 00:37:59,720
Have you watched the video?

607
00:37:59,800 --> 00:38:01,600
- Dare to?
- No, thanks.

608
00:38:01,680 --> 00:38:04,040
I'd die of embarrassment.

609
00:38:04,680 --> 00:38:05,640
I'll take your word for it.

610
00:38:07,040 --> 00:38:09,760
- Hey, hey.
- There she is!

611
00:38:15,320 --> 00:38:16,840
That's my friend!

612
00:38:17,440 --> 00:38:18,600
Proud!

613
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:33,280
<i>We're sitting and gazing</i>
<i>At the sky together just like always</i>

614
00:38:33,360 --> 00:38:37,400
<i>But the feelings I have inside</i>
<i>Have changed</i>

615
00:38:37,480 --> 00:38:39,120
Why does your camera
always drift toward Proud?

616
00:38:40,240 --> 00:38:41,320
Quit calling me out.

617
00:38:43,880 --> 00:38:48,520
<i>Why does it feel so good</i>
<i>Whenever I'm close to you?</i>

618
00:38:48,600 --> 00:38:53,320
<i>I still don't know</i>
<i>If you feel the same way</i>

619
00:38:53,400 --> 00:38:55,640
Here, let me film it. I'm the taller one.

620
00:38:55,720 --> 00:38:57,280
<i>Like this</i>

621
00:38:57,360 --> 00:39:02,760
<i>The closer I get</i>
<i>The more I start to fall</i>

622
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:07,760
<i>The closer I am to you</i>
<i>The better it feels every time</i>

623
00:39:07,840 --> 00:39:12,600
<i>Is this what love feels like?</i>

624
00:39:12,680 --> 00:39:15,040
<i>Should I just be a good friend</i>

625
00:39:15,120 --> 00:39:18,920
<i>Or should I speak up</i>
<i>And say I love you?</i>

626
00:39:32,240 --> 00:39:34,040
Hey! Indy!

627
00:39:34,720 --> 00:39:35,560
You came?

628
00:39:35,640 --> 00:39:37,560
- Damn!
- Hey!

629
00:39:37,640 --> 00:39:39,040
You look amazing today.

630
00:39:39,120 --> 00:39:41,080
Looking handsome. What did you do?

631
00:39:41,160 --> 00:39:43,200
Jia deserves the credit.

632
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:46,360
Today, we also have our friends

633
00:39:46,440 --> 00:39:48,320
from Lazy Meow Meow with us.

634
00:39:53,360 --> 00:39:58,040
A big round of applause
for Indy and LeeIth!

635
00:40:00,720 --> 00:40:03,840
- Damn, it took forever to get here.
- Where's your mom?

636
00:40:03,920 --> 00:40:05,440
- Where did she go?
- Forget about my mom.

637
00:40:05,520 --> 00:40:06,680
- We've been waiting forever.
- I rushed over.

638
00:40:06,760 --> 00:40:07,640
Hey, teacher… I mean,

639
00:40:07,720 --> 00:40:08,680
Jia, you're here too?

640
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:10,280
Man, I missed you. It's been a while.

641
00:40:10,360 --> 00:40:11,560
- Putter, hey.
- Hey.

642
00:40:11,640 --> 00:40:13,440
Hey, Summer. Hey, Yihwa.

643
00:40:13,520 --> 00:40:14,400
Hey, Min.

644
00:40:14,480 --> 00:40:15,880
Hi.

645
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:19,000
Let's hear it for Lazy Meow Meow!

646
00:40:23,880 --> 00:40:27,720
<i>I've been in love with you for so long</i>

647
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:31,320
<i>I want to tell you, I want to tell you</i>
<i>But I never have the guts</i>

648
00:40:31,400 --> 00:40:36,560
<i>I'm glad that today</i>
<i>You'll finally know that</i>

649
00:40:36,640 --> 00:40:38,920
<i>It's just that, it's just that</i>

650
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:42,800
<i>I don't want to be just friends anymore</i>
<i>Let me be more than that</i>

651
00:40:42,880 --> 00:40:44,720
<i>There's only you, only you</i>

652
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:46,600
<i>I wish we loved each other</i>

653
00:40:46,680 --> 00:40:51,920
<i>I want you to know that today</i>

654
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:54,120
<i>I don't want to be</i>
<i>Just your friend anymore</i>

655
00:40:54,200 --> 00:40:56,560
<i>The one standing next to that guy.</i>

656
00:40:57,160 --> 00:40:58,320
The one with the big eyes.

657
00:40:58,400 --> 00:41:00,960
He's so damn cute when he smiles.

658
00:41:01,600 --> 00:41:03,120
Yeah, he's cute.

659
00:41:22,520 --> 00:41:27,080
<i>I really don't know</i>
<i>If you feel the same way</i>

660
00:41:27,160 --> 00:41:30,200
<i>If I say it out loud, will I lose you?</i>

661
00:41:35,120 --> 00:41:36,400
Damn.

662
00:41:37,080 --> 00:41:39,120
Why does his camera keep pointing at me?

663
00:41:41,960 --> 00:41:43,280
I'd better search it.

664
00:41:48,520 --> 00:41:51,440
WHY DOES MY HEART RACE
AROUND MY BEST FRIEND?

665
00:41:55,360 --> 00:41:56,440
Too long.

666
00:42:02,480 --> 00:42:04,040
<i>A racing heart around a friend</i>

667
00:42:04,120 --> 00:42:05,720
<i>can be caused by psychology or hormones.</i>

668
00:42:06,560 --> 00:42:07,800
Hormones?

669
00:42:09,080 --> 00:42:10,600
Psychology?

670
00:42:11,680 --> 00:42:13,920
- And…
<i>- Or feelings beyond friendship.</i>

671
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:16,280
No way.

672
00:42:16,360 --> 00:42:18,240
We're just friends, aren't we?

673
00:42:25,960 --> 00:42:27,520
Why were you in the bathroom so long?

674
00:42:28,560 --> 00:42:30,960
- What's with you?
- I'm fine.

675
00:42:31,040 --> 00:42:32,200
That's my business, isn't it?

676
00:42:34,600 --> 00:42:36,000
What's with him?

677
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:43,400
Why didn't he turn off the tap?

678
00:42:59,520 --> 00:43:00,960
Pull it in, Tun.

679
00:43:01,040 --> 00:43:02,520
Nice.

680
00:43:05,560 --> 00:43:06,640
Too weak.

681
00:43:07,600 --> 00:43:09,080
I was flirting with their side.

682
00:43:10,760 --> 00:43:11,880
Then don't flirt too much.

683
00:43:19,760 --> 00:43:21,280
Why?

684
00:43:21,360 --> 00:43:22,600
Afraid you'll fall for me?

685
00:43:29,720 --> 00:43:32,000
No, you'll make us lose.

686
00:43:32,080 --> 00:43:33,600
Then I'll lose all my stars.

687
00:43:39,920 --> 00:43:41,440
You haven't eaten?

688
00:43:42,000 --> 00:43:45,440
Yeah. I was too excited tonight,
so I skipped dinner.

689
00:43:47,520 --> 00:43:48,880
I'll cook for you.

690
00:43:50,400 --> 00:43:51,680
Then we'll be even.

691
00:44:03,720 --> 00:44:05,280
Done!

692
00:44:06,080 --> 00:44:08,080
Presented by the son of an Iron Chef.

693
00:44:09,600 --> 00:44:11,600
Railway fried rice.

694
00:44:13,120 --> 00:44:14,160
It looks pretty good.

695
00:44:16,160 --> 00:44:17,720
How does it taste?

696
00:44:25,680 --> 00:44:26,680
Well?

697
00:44:27,760 --> 00:44:29,200
Be honest with me.

698
00:44:30,480 --> 00:44:32,360
Honestly,

699
00:44:32,440 --> 00:44:34,520
- It's not very good.
- Really?

700
00:44:38,480 --> 00:44:39,480
It's not that good.

701
00:44:39,560 --> 00:44:41,480
Is your mom really a chef?

702
00:44:43,720 --> 00:44:44,880
Let me try it.

703
00:44:50,600 --> 00:44:51,560
Well?

704
00:44:51,640 --> 00:44:53,000
I'm screwed.

705
00:44:53,960 --> 00:44:55,600
I didn't even taste it first.

706
00:44:55,680 --> 00:44:57,720
I was a little too confident.

707
00:44:59,640 --> 00:45:02,200
Honestly, it would probably be fine
with a fried egg.

708
00:45:02,880 --> 00:45:04,600
It's okay. You don't have to eat it.

709
00:45:04,680 --> 00:45:06,120
I'll order you something instead.

710
00:45:06,800 --> 00:45:08,000
It's fine.

711
00:45:21,040 --> 00:45:22,960
Are you eating it just to cheer me up?

712
00:45:26,160 --> 00:45:27,520
It's edible.

713
00:45:28,880 --> 00:45:30,080
But yeah.

714
00:45:32,520 --> 00:45:34,400
You told me to cheer you up, didn't you?

715
00:45:42,520 --> 00:45:43,840
Thanks.

716
00:45:43,920 --> 00:45:46,200
I'll do better next time.

717
00:45:48,400 --> 00:45:50,600
I'm going to bed.

718
00:45:52,400 --> 00:45:53,520
Hey, not yet.

719
00:45:53,600 --> 00:45:55,920
You'll get acid reflux if you
sleep right after eating.

720
00:45:56,640 --> 00:45:58,480
Sir, I know that.

721
00:45:58,560 --> 00:46:00,160
I'll sit around for a while first.

722
00:46:00,240 --> 00:46:01,440
Yeah. Thank you.

723
00:46:01,520 --> 00:46:02,680
Bye.

724
00:46:29,760 --> 00:46:31,000
You've got a lot of stuff.

725
00:46:32,480 --> 00:46:33,720
Yeah.

726
00:46:33,800 --> 00:46:35,720
They told us to bring the props.

727
00:46:35,800 --> 00:46:38,360
Here, let me carry this.

728
00:46:38,440 --> 00:46:39,640
I want to look cool.

729
00:46:40,720 --> 00:46:42,520
Not sure about that.

730
00:46:43,440 --> 00:46:44,800
You talk too much.

731
00:46:44,880 --> 00:46:46,400
Not even a thank you?

732
00:46:47,280 --> 00:46:49,760
Alright, thanks.

733
00:47:16,320 --> 00:47:17,320
Damn!

734
00:47:19,200 --> 00:47:20,200
Get out!

735
00:47:20,920 --> 00:47:21,760
You're so slow.

736
00:47:21,840 --> 00:47:23,600
You'll get what's coming.

737
00:47:37,040 --> 00:47:39,120
Hey, where are you rushing off to?

738
00:47:39,200 --> 00:47:40,280
The crosswalk's right here.

739
00:47:40,360 --> 00:47:41,680
PLEASE WAIT FOR WALK SIGNAL

740
00:47:41,760 --> 00:47:44,240
Crossing here is basically the same.

741
00:47:44,320 --> 00:47:47,080
- It's faster, too.
- But the crosswalk's safer.

742
00:47:47,680 --> 00:47:48,680
Let's go.

743
00:47:52,240 --> 00:47:53,280
PLEASE WAIT FOR WALK SIGNAL

744
00:48:06,960 --> 00:48:08,600
Were you worried about me?

745
00:48:10,480 --> 00:48:11,560
Yeah.

746
00:48:13,640 --> 00:48:14,920
If you'd gotten hit,

747
00:48:15,000 --> 00:48:16,640
I'd have to take responsibility again.

748
00:48:16,720 --> 00:48:18,360
Your mom would kill me.

749
00:48:19,040 --> 00:48:21,760
Besides, if you crossed there,

750
00:48:22,360 --> 00:48:23,520
you would hold up traffic.

751
00:48:23,600 --> 00:48:25,640
You'd be the one causing traffic in Siam.

752
00:48:27,560 --> 00:48:29,560
Alright, Dad.

753
00:48:29,640 --> 00:48:31,440
I gave in the moment you said, "Yeah."

754
00:48:33,480 --> 00:48:34,440
Oh, right.

755
00:48:34,520 --> 00:48:36,280
Can you go somewhere with me after school?

756
00:48:38,360 --> 00:48:40,320
Sure. Let's go.

757
00:48:50,800 --> 00:48:52,800
Damn. It's beautiful.

758
00:48:52,880 --> 00:48:55,000
It does look nice.

759
00:49:00,320 --> 00:49:02,440
Hold on. That's 10,000 baht.

760
00:49:02,520 --> 00:49:04,320
If you spend that much,

761
00:49:04,400 --> 00:49:05,320
I'm telling your mom.

762
00:49:06,000 --> 00:49:08,960
I'm not scared. It's my savings.

763
00:49:09,040 --> 00:49:10,040
I can buy whatever I want.

764
00:49:13,440 --> 00:49:16,000
I know the more expensive the headphones,

765
00:49:16,080 --> 00:49:18,120
the better they are,
but is it really necessary?

766
00:49:18,200 --> 00:49:19,680
Of course it is.

767
00:49:19,760 --> 00:49:22,680
This way,
I can practice without disturbing you.

768
00:49:22,760 --> 00:49:23,960
Look at Tae.

769
00:49:24,040 --> 00:49:26,920
He stepped on mine and broke it.

770
00:49:36,600 --> 00:49:40,040
So, you haven't practiced music
at all these past two weeks?

771
00:49:41,400 --> 00:49:43,480
I didn't want to bother you
since you were studying for finals.

772
00:49:44,160 --> 00:49:45,160
And playing games too.

773
00:50:07,720 --> 00:50:10,920
Damn, this is so good. Give it a listen.

774
00:50:29,440 --> 00:50:30,280
It's pretty good.

775
00:50:32,560 --> 00:50:34,000
Told you.

776
00:50:56,440 --> 00:50:58,720
<i>If the rule is not to fall</i>
<i>for someone close to you,</i>

777
00:50:58,800 --> 00:51:00,000
<i>then does that mean…?</i>

778
00:51:00,840 --> 00:51:02,400
<i>I wish I could take a tour of your mind.</i>

779
00:51:02,480 --> 00:51:03,840
<i>To see what you're thinking.</i>

780
00:51:07,840 --> 00:51:09,120
<i>When I said I was laughing,</i>

781
00:51:09,200 --> 00:51:11,880
<i>actually, I think I was just embarrassed.</i>

782
00:51:11,960 --> 00:51:13,480
I DON'T THINK #TERLEEITH ARE JUST FRIENDS.

783
00:51:13,560 --> 00:51:14,880
DOES PUTTER SMILE LIKE THAT TO EVERYONE
OR JUST LEEITH?

784
00:51:14,960 --> 00:51:16,080
GUYS, I WANT TO ANNOUNCE THAT PUTTER
IS LEEITH'S BOYFRIEND. END OF DISCUSSION.

785
00:51:16,160 --> 00:51:17,160
LEEITH AND PUTTER ARE ROOMMATES
BUT KEPT IT FROM THEIR CLUB FRIENDS.

786
00:51:17,240 --> 00:51:18,400
THEY'RE JUST SITTING BESIDE EACH OTHER
AND HERE I AM WRITING THEIR WEDDING SCENE.

787
00:51:18,480 --> 00:51:19,600
GET #TERLEEITH OUT OF MY HEAD.
I HAVE AN EXAM COMING UP.

788
00:51:19,680 --> 00:51:20,960
WHEN THEY MAKE IT OFFICIAL, I'LL SET OFF
FIREWORKS NEAR THE PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE.

789
00:51:21,040 --> 00:51:22,360
YOU CAN SUE ME FOR BEING DELULU,
BUT I SAW THEM BEING SO ROMANTIC TODAY.

790
00:51:26,280 --> 00:51:27,920
<i>If you have a crush on your friend,</i>

791
00:51:28,000 --> 00:51:29,880
<i>should you tell them or not?</i>

792
00:51:49,200 --> 00:51:50,200
NOWADAYS, IF YOU LIKE SOMEONE,
JUST TELL THEM.

793
00:51:50,280 --> 00:51:51,400
IF IT DOESN'T WORK OUT,
YOU'LL MOVE ON SOON ENOUGH.

794
00:51:51,480 --> 00:51:52,440
THAT'S HOW WE STARTED.
IF I HADN'T CONFESSED

795
00:51:52,520 --> 00:51:53,440
THAT DAY, WE WOULDN'T BE WHERE WE ARE NOW.

796
00:51:53,520 --> 00:51:54,520
I HOPE THE ANSWER
IS WHAT YOU'RE WISHING FOR.

797
00:51:54,600 --> 00:51:55,600
YOU'LL NEVER KNOW UNLESS YOU TRY.

798
00:51:55,680 --> 00:51:56,680
JUST HAVING THE COURAGE TO EXPRESS

799
00:51:56,760 --> 00:51:57,800
YOUR FEELINGS IS ALREADY
AMAZING. YOU GOT THIS!

800
00:51:57,880 --> 00:51:58,800
HOPE "FRIEND" TURNS INTO "BOYFRIEND."

801
00:51:58,880 --> 00:52:03,880
GO FOR IT. I'M ROOTING FOR YOU.
I'LL BE WAITING FOR AN UPDATE.

802
00:52:24,160 --> 00:52:25,400
<i>Are you at Siam?</i>

803
00:52:31,520 --> 00:52:33,200
I didn't think you'd message me.

804
00:52:33,280 --> 00:52:35,120
I thought you were on Summer's side.

805
00:52:35,920 --> 00:52:37,480
I'm staying neutral.

806
00:52:37,560 --> 00:52:40,120
So, are you two still mad at each other?

807
00:52:40,920 --> 00:52:42,960
I'm over it, but she isn't.

808
00:52:43,040 --> 00:52:44,800
I'm figuring out how to make it up to her.

809
00:52:44,880 --> 00:52:46,960
Alright, I'll help.

810
00:52:47,040 --> 00:52:48,200
Let's deal with your problem first.

811
00:52:48,280 --> 00:52:50,120
So, what do you want to ask your big sis?

812
00:52:53,480 --> 00:52:54,400
It's about love, isn't it?

813
00:52:56,360 --> 00:52:57,480
Damn,

814
00:52:57,560 --> 00:52:59,080
- How did you know?
- I'm good, right?

815
00:52:59,760 --> 00:53:00,760
You're the best, Sis.

816
00:53:00,840 --> 00:53:02,080
So, what's going on?

817
00:53:08,160 --> 00:53:10,080
What made you…

818
00:53:10,840 --> 00:53:12,080
confess to Summer?

819
00:53:14,680 --> 00:53:16,600
It sounds cliché, but…

820
00:53:16,680 --> 00:53:18,560
I was afraid I'd regret not telling her.

821
00:53:34,640 --> 00:53:36,000
Want me to help?

822
00:53:44,880 --> 00:53:47,560
<i>Back in Grade 8, Summer said</i>
<i>she was transferring schools.</i>

823
00:53:49,480 --> 00:53:52,640
<i>Every day, I felt more and more uneasy.</i>

824
00:53:53,520 --> 00:53:56,200
<i>I was afraid she'd never be</i>
<i>the same if I told her.</i>

825
00:54:00,600 --> 00:54:03,480
<i>But I was even more afraid</i>
<i>I'd regret it forever if I didn't.</i>

826
00:54:10,440 --> 00:54:11,760
<i>So I realized…</i>

827
00:54:12,360 --> 00:54:14,040
<i>I was more afraid of regretting it.</i>

828
00:54:15,440 --> 00:54:16,720
Look over there.

829
00:54:17,440 --> 00:54:18,320
Look.

830
00:54:25,280 --> 00:54:26,840
There's something I want to tell you.

831
00:54:33,720 --> 00:54:35,320
Let's be together, Summer.

832
00:54:39,600 --> 00:54:40,880
So, is that a yes?

833
00:54:45,480 --> 00:54:48,680
<i>It turned out to be</i>
<i>the best decision of my life.</i>

834
00:54:54,920 --> 00:54:56,560
Why are you two so romantic?

835
00:54:57,320 --> 00:54:59,760
That's how Wattanakanlaya's top
couple does it.

836
00:55:15,240 --> 00:55:16,200
I think I have my answer now.

837
00:55:16,800 --> 00:55:18,800
Then I'll be waiting to see what happens.

838
00:55:21,240 --> 00:55:22,800
Thank you so much, Sis.

839
00:55:22,880 --> 00:55:24,160
Thank you so much.

840
00:55:25,200 --> 00:55:26,680
Alright, I'm off.

841
00:55:47,800 --> 00:55:50,400
Hey, I have something to tell you.

842
00:57:09,760 --> 00:57:10,800
Hey.

843
00:57:11,720 --> 00:57:12,880
Pay attention in class.

844
00:57:34,800 --> 00:57:37,600
<i>Hey, I have something to tell you.</i>

845
00:57:43,280 --> 00:57:44,600
I'm sorry.

846
00:57:45,280 --> 00:57:47,000
For not telling you in person.

847
00:57:50,000 --> 00:57:51,520
I wasn't brave enough,

848
00:57:54,160 --> 00:57:55,880
because I was afraid of your reaction.

849
00:57:57,160 --> 00:58:00,280
<i>I wanted to thank you</i>

850
00:58:02,440 --> 00:58:05,240
<i>for always looking after me,</i>
<i>caring about me,</i>

851
00:58:06,480 --> 00:58:10,000
<i>and making me feel so comfortable</i>
<i>being myself.</i>

852
00:58:13,520 --> 00:58:15,440
After saying all of that,

853
00:58:15,520 --> 00:58:16,800
what I really want to tell you is…

854
00:58:33,040 --> 00:58:34,720
I like you.

855
00:58:34,800 --> 00:58:37,560
Break that rule and be my boyfriend.

856
00:58:39,880 --> 00:58:42,720
<i>Shit. What the hell am I saying?</i>

857
01:00:08,640 --> 01:00:09,640
Damn it.

858
01:00:30,120 --> 01:00:31,120
Why didn't you answer my calls?

859
01:00:35,240 --> 01:00:37,320
My phone died, and I forgot my charger.

860
01:00:41,680 --> 01:00:42,800
Well…

861
01:00:46,040 --> 01:00:47,000
I listened to it.

862
01:00:48,800 --> 01:00:52,080
You did? So, what do you think?

863
01:00:55,800 --> 01:00:57,400
After I heard it,

864
01:00:59,280 --> 01:01:01,680
I finally realized who

865
01:01:01,760 --> 01:01:05,080
the reading meant when it said
someone would confess to you.

866
01:01:07,800 --> 01:01:09,000
Who?

867
01:01:13,160 --> 01:01:14,440
Me.

868
01:01:15,240 --> 01:01:18,520
And now I'm sure that reading was right.

869
01:01:19,760 --> 01:01:22,920
I've… been fighting the voice
in my head for so long.

870
01:01:25,760 --> 01:01:26,920
But today…

871
01:01:28,360 --> 01:01:30,200
I think I'm done fighting it.

872
01:01:34,200 --> 01:01:35,920
What did that voice say?

873
01:01:41,040 --> 01:01:42,320
Well…

874
01:01:43,600 --> 01:01:45,320
Will you give me a chance?

875
01:01:49,440 --> 01:01:50,520
As your boyfriend.

876
01:01:57,400 --> 01:01:59,320
I'm ready to break the rule.

877
01:02:00,480 --> 01:02:01,320
What about you?

878
01:02:12,360 --> 01:02:13,680
If I wasn't ready to break the rule,

879
01:02:14,360 --> 01:02:16,600
why would I record
that confession on your laptop?

880
01:02:18,440 --> 01:02:20,840
So, you…

881
01:02:20,920 --> 01:02:22,840
I'm saying yes.

882
01:02:22,920 --> 01:02:24,560
Don't be so clueless now.

883
01:02:32,760 --> 01:02:33,760
Here.

884
01:02:34,520 --> 01:02:36,720
A gift for our first day together.

885
01:02:37,240 --> 01:02:39,000
It was buy one, get one free.

886
01:02:50,040 --> 01:02:51,240
Damn, what did I just say?

887
01:02:55,720 --> 01:02:56,640
Hey,

888
01:02:57,520 --> 01:02:59,040
why are you hiding from me?

889
01:02:59,560 --> 01:03:01,400
I want to see you blush.

890
01:03:02,200 --> 01:03:03,480
Alright, alright. Let's go.

891
01:03:03,560 --> 01:03:05,320
Let's head back to our room.

892
01:03:06,240 --> 01:03:07,320
Our room?

893
01:03:07,400 --> 01:03:08,840
Don't get all cheesy.

894
01:03:16,840 --> 01:03:18,040
What are you doing?

895
01:03:22,600 --> 01:03:24,680
"Our first-day-together gift."

896
01:03:24,760 --> 01:03:25,680
Not cheesy at all, huh?

897
01:03:26,720 --> 01:03:28,680
That's enough.
I'm not listening. Let's go.

898
01:03:28,760 --> 01:03:30,320
Let's head back.

899
01:03:30,400 --> 01:03:32,000
Yeah, let's go.

900
01:03:32,080 --> 01:03:34,240
- Hey, wait for me!
- Come on, let's go.

901
01:04:09,560 --> 01:04:11,000
Make it look natural.

902
01:04:11,080 --> 01:04:12,280
<i>Yeah, yeah.</i>

903
01:04:14,400 --> 01:04:16,000
Putter.

904
01:04:17,000 --> 01:04:18,200
<i>Werewolf, close your eyes.</i>

905
01:04:19,600 --> 01:04:20,880
You like this one.

906
01:04:20,960 --> 01:04:23,240
<i>Is there anything you're hiding from me?</i>

907
01:04:23,320 --> 01:04:25,200
- <i>No.</i>
- You've been lonely lately.

908
01:04:25,280 --> 01:04:26,840
Feeling neglected and suspicious.

909
01:04:27,440 --> 01:04:29,160
<i>If you don't want me</i>
<i>as your friend anymore,</i>

910
01:04:29,240 --> 01:04:31,160
<i>just say it, damn it.</i>

911
01:04:32,120 --> 01:04:33,000
<i>Is that a new perfume?</i>

912
01:04:33,080 --> 01:04:34,240
That's the same scent Indy wears.

913
01:04:34,320 --> 01:04:36,120
<i>LeeIth, have you seen this?</i>

914
01:04:36,200 --> 01:04:38,000
<i>The Brain Drain Gang found</i>
<i>Putter's secret account.</i>
